    {
      "run": 2,
      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "Upon entering the cramped galley, I found myself enveloped in the salty aroma of the sea, which seemed to have seeped into every corner of the space. My goal was to explore and understand this part of the ship better, but it quickly became clear that the primary focus here was on cooking and perhaps storage, as indicated by the presence of the kettle resting on the floor. This simple piece of equipment, made of tin and dented on one side, did not yield easily to my curiosity, for it could not be opened. Despite its seemingly mundane nature, the kettle seemed to encapsulate the essence of life aboard this vessel, where functionality often triumphs over ornate adornment. The overall atmosphere in the galley, saturated with salt, instantly transported me to the world of seafaring, where survival and necessity dictate existence.",
