    {
      "run": 4,
      "steps": 12,
      "narrative": "Upon entering the ship, the cramped galley immediately caught my attention, its salt-infused air and sparse furnishings offering a stark contrast to the bustling activity I imagined aboard. With a sense of curiosity, I examined a kettle on the floor, finding it dented and covered in salt, indicative of its regular use. While I initially picked it up, the thought crossed my mind that it might be more useful to someone who could fully utilize it, so I decided to put it down. My exploration led me to a storeroom where I found a stiff coil of rope, which I took a moment to examine before deciding it was best to leave it behind, possibly for tasks that required more secure bindings. Carrying no items as I left the store, I reflect on the simplicity of the tasks undertaken during this visit, each decision made with consideration for the practicality of the tools I encountered.",
